The bug was caused by the use of deprecated GTK functions and types in the code, specifically the use of `gtk_hbox_new` and `gtk_vbox_new`, which were replaced by `gtk_box_new` in GTK version 3.0. The patch corrects these issues by ensuring that the appropriate functions are used based on the GTK version, thus fixing the UI issues that arose from the incorrect widget creation methods.
